{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795219,"nonce":"UhljK/XvPp4HhH/05uA6T4zMRPE=","title":"Define Jam protocol, ownership and extension service contracts","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P0\n\nScope\nDesign the versioned client/backend protocol and domain schemas for events, rooms, documents, participants, roles, publication consent and one explicit billing owner. Specify message/request/update IDs, error envelopes, supported-version negotiation, shared-root file manifests, join/reconnect state, per-document lazy loading, deadlines/cancellation and byte/count limits. Separate identity, room authority, media state, driver state and entitlements. Describe the proposed RayScript service/provider contracts without exposing backend secrets or native pointers.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nA reviewable wire/schema contract covers happy path and incompatible versions, invalid/oversized input, replay, permission rejection and room closure. Native/browser fixtures can exchange conformance messages. A self-hostable alternate backend can implement the public protocol without changing editor state schemas. There is no hidden assumption that a Durable Object merges edits or that a provider account grants room membership.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}